Every time I ship a landing page, client site, or side project, the same boring issues slip through if I check them manually: Missing Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS), X-Frame-Options, or X-Content-Type-Options
Broken og:image previews or missing <link rel="canonical"> when shared on social media A TLS certificate silently nearing expiration on a custom domain An accidental http:// mixed-content script or image on an HTTPS page A 404 internal link introduced by a last-minute route rename You do not need a bloated SaaS subscription just to catch these before launch. Here is the minimal, copy-paste workflow I use. Most static hosts and reverse proxies leave baseline security headers unset by default. _headers)
/* Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains X-Cont…

Selling a digital download through BTCPay is easy right up to the delivery step. BTCPay can create the invoice, but it does not inherently know how to release a private zip after payment.
I needed this for a small static store. The constraints were:
static product pages;
BTCPay Point of Sale invoices;
no customer accounts;
no email-required delivery;
no database;
no trusting a browser redirect as proof of payment;
automatic delivery after confirmation.
I packaged the result as an open-source Netlify template:
btcpay-digital-fulfillment
static HTML form
  -> BTCPay POS invoice
  -> buyer pays
  -> BTCPay redirect template with {InvoiceId}
  -> Netlify Function checks Greenfield invoice status
  -> zip download only when status is Settled

